{"type": "dashboard", "id": "s2_ato-dashboard", "coreMigrationVersion": "8.8.0", "typeMigrationVersion": "10.1.0", "attributes": {"title": "S2_ATO \u2014 Credential Harvesting & Online-Banking Account Takeover", "description": "Credential Harvesting & Online-Banking Account Takeover. v7 promotion model: base alert severity (0\u2013100, same formula as baseline) owns the base tier; the PII context is a bounded, weighted promotion layer that ADDS three visible contributions \u2014 PII exposure (0\u201325, impact), asset criticality (0\u201320, impact), attack complexity (0\u201315, likelihood) \u2014 so enriched risk = base + the three. Impact (\u226445) outweighs likelihood (\u226415): a confirmed attack on Tier-1/2 PII is promoted to critical, a sophisticated attack on non-PII data is capped at high; critical is gated on a confirmed PII attack (Tier-1/2 PII target AND observed PII exposure or \u22651 correlated technique). The \u2018Escalation Contribution by Priority\u2019 chart decomposes each tier's score into these four parts \u2014 the defensible evidence for the high\u2192critical promotion. Bands: green<40 low \u00b7 yellow 40\u201360 medium \u00b7 orange 60\u201380 high \u00b7 red 80+ critical. Bottom rows contrast baseline vs enriched priority distribution against ground truth, and decompose the enriched critical tier into true positives (green, malicious) vs false positives (red, benign authorized bulk exports).", "panelsJSON": "[{\"type\": \"lens\", \"gridData\": {\"i\": \"s2_ato-composite\", \"x\": 0, \"y\": 0, \"w\": 48, \"h\": 16}, \"panelIndex\": \"s2_ato-composite\", \"embeddableConfig\": {\"enhancements\": {}}, \"panelRefName\": \"panel_0\"}, {\"type\": \"lens\", \"gridData\": {\"i\": \"s2_ato-breakdown\", \"x\": 0, \"y\": 16, \"w\": 48, \"h\": 18}, \"panelIndex\": \"s2_ato-breakdown\", \"embeddableConfig\": {\"enhancements\": {}}, \"panelRefName\": \"panel_1\"}, {\"type\": \"lens\", \"gridData\": {\"i\": \"s2_ato-base\", \"x\": 0, \"y\": 34, \"w\":